You should never go down the stairs while *wielding* a cockatrice
corpse. In fact, you should never move while wielding a cockatrice
corpse; if you want to move *at all* unwield it, even when you're
*completely sure* there aren't any pits where you want to go.

A cockatrice corpse in your inventory that you're not wielding is
completely harmless, as long as you don't eat it by mistake or try to
wield it when you're not wearing your gloves (for instance because
something has stolen or disintegrated them, or you've taken them off
for some reason).

That a cockatrice corpse in your inventory, not wielded, is dangerous is
a NetHack myth that deserves to be trampled into the earth.

By the way, the true message is "Falling, you touch the cockatrice
corpse." A falling cockatrice corpse will only petrify you when it
falls on your head after you've thrown it into the air; "petrified by
elementary physics" (i.e. what goes up must come down).

   Raisse, killed by tasting cockatrice meat

